	"label": "cup-inside — editable vegetation material",
	"longdesc": "",
	"name": "cup-inside",
	"node_position": {
		"x": 0.0,
		"y": 0.0
	},
	"nodes": [
		{
			"color": {
				"a": 1.0,
				"b": 0.300000011920929,
				"g": 0.239999994635582,
				"r": 0.140000000596046,
				"type": "Color"
			},
			"name": "About",
			"node_position": {
				"x": 0.0,
				"y": -350.0
			},
			"parameters": {},
			"seed": -350.0,
			"size": {
				"x": 900.0,
				"y": 214.0
			},
			"text": "Photographic material: the inside of a large cup fungus, its fleshy ridges and fine veins running along the cup from its foot to its lip, from a photographic study (tools/materials/plant_sources.py bark), built from sources/ (pigment and the 16-bit height fields). The models' UVs set the ground one repeat covers, and their vertex colours tint the light grey pigment (orange-red to a paler lip). Pigment/SoftenRidges compresses the study's contrast so the bowl's shading and rounded lip lead over the ridges at the board's iso scale; the relief is kept low for the same reason. Glow colorizes the ridges' height into a soft emission: the fungal gills glow warm, and the game makes the glow pulse slowly across a colony. The sources tile seamlessly: keep them so. Relief is the heightmap's height range as a percentage of the repeat; the normals round it to a whole code of the heightmap (Relief x 25.5), so keep it a multiple of 10 / 255 (0.0392), and set the Material node's Depth scale to Relief / 25 (tools/materials/README.md). The ...PNG8 groups and the nodes after them only store exact file values; leave them. Export: File > Export material > Godot > Godot 4 Standard into data/models/board/textures/vegetation/fungus, then Reload assets in the game's Tuning panel.",
			"title": "About this material",
			"type": "comment"
		},
